messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 614 and 332?\nI think the correct answer is: 203948\n# Reasoning:", '<think>\nI need to figure out what is the product of 614 and 332. First, I will align the numbers based on place value, writing one number above the other.\n\nNext, I will multiply each digit of the bottom number by each digit of the top number, starting from the rightmost digit of the bottom number.\n\nI will write each resulting partial product in its correct place value, shifting one position to the left for each new row.\n\nIf the product of any two digits is greater than 9, I will carry over the extra value to the next place value.\n\nI will continue this process until all digits have been multiplied.\n\nFinally, I will add all the partial products together to obtain the final product.</think>\nTherefore, the answer is ']]
