      "text": "80686.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Multiply 487 by 8 (ones place of 178):**\n   - 7 \u00d7 8 = 56. Write down 6 and carry over 5.\n   - 8 \u00d7 8 = 64, plus the carried 5 equals 69. Write down 9 and carry over 6.\n   - 4 \u00d7 8 = 32, plus the carried 6 equals 38. Write down 38.\n   - **Partial Product:** 3,896\n\n2. **Multiply 487 by 70 (tens place of 178):**\n   - 7 \u00d7 7 = 49. Write down 9 and carry over 4.\n   - 8 \u00d7 7 = 56, plus the carried 4 equals 60. Write down 0 and carry over 6.\n   - 4 \u00d7 7 = 28, plus the carried 6 equals 34. Write down 34.\n   - **Partial Product:** 34,090\n\n3. **Multiply 487 by 100 (hundreds place of 178):**\n   - 487 \u00d7 100 = 48,700\n   - **Partial Product:** 48,700\n\n4. **Add all partial products together:**\n   - 3,896 + 34,090 + 48,700 = 86,686\n\n**Final Answer:** 86,686\n\nHowever, the initial thought of 80,686 is incorrect. The correct product of 487 and 178 is 86,686.\n\n```plaintext\n   487\n\u00d7 178\n-------\n   3896  (487 \u00d7 8)\n 34090   (487 \u00d7 70)\n48700    (487 \u00d7 100)\n-------\n 86686\n```\n\n**Final Answer:** 86,686",
