      "text": "572456.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Multiply 734 by 4 (ones place of 784):**\n   - 4 \u00d7 4 = 16. Write down 6 and carry over 1.\n   - 4 \u00d7 3 = 12, plus the carried 1 equals 13. Write down 3 and carry over 1.\n   - 4 \u00d7 7 = 28, plus the carried 1 equals 29. Write down 29.\n   - **Partial Product:** 2936\n\n2. **Multiply 734 by 80 (tens place of 784):**\n   - 8 \u00d7 4 = 32. Write down 2 and carry over 3.\n   - 8 \u00d7 3 = 24, plus the carried 3 equals 27. Write down 7 and carry over 2.\n   - 8 \u00d7 7 = 56, plus the carried 2 equals 58. Write down 58.\n   - **Partial Product:** 58720\n\n3. **Multiply 734 by 700 (hundreds place of 784):**\n   - 7 \u00d7 4 = 28. Write down 8 and carry over 2.\n   - 7 \u00d7 3 = 21, plus the carried 2 equals 23. Write down 3 and carry over 2.\n   - 7 \u00d7 7 = 49, plus the carried 2 equals 51. Write down 51.\n   - **Partial Product:** 513800\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   - 2936 + 58720 = 61656\n   - 61656 + 513800 = 575456\n\n**Final Answer:** 575456\n\nHowever, upon reviewing the calculation, there seems to be a discrepancy. The correct product of 734 and 784 is actually 575,456, not 572,456 as initially thought.\n\n**Corrected Final Answer:** 575456",
