      "text": "370240.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Multiply 720 by 2 (ones place of 542):**\n   - 720 \u00d7 2 = 1,440\n\n2. **Multiply 720 by 40 (tens place of 542):**\n   - 720 \u00d7 40 = 28,800\n\n3. **Multiply 720 by 500 (hundreds place of 542):**\n   - 720 \u00d7 500 = 360,000\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   - 1,440 + 28,800 + 360,000 = 390,240\n\n**Final Answer:**\nThe product of 720 and 542 is **390,240**.\n\n```plaintext\n   720\n\u00d7 542\n------\n  1440   (720 \u00d7 2)\n 28800   (720 \u00d7 40)\n360000   (720 \u00d7 500)\n------\n390240\n```\n\n**Final Answer:** \\boxed{390240}\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 720 and 542, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 720 by 2 (ones place of 542):**\n   \\[\n   720 \\times 2 = 1,\\!440\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 720 by 40 (tens place of 542):**\n   \\[\n   720 \\times 40 = 28,\\!800\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 720 by 500 (hundreds place of 542):**\n   \\[\n   720 \\times 500 = 360,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   1,\\!440 + 28,\\!800 + 360,\\!000 = 390,\\!240\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\\[\n\\boxed{390240}\n\\]",
