      "text": "422168.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Multiply 616 by 3 (ones place of 523):**\n   - 6 \u00d7 3 = 18\n   - 1 \u00d7 3 = 3 (plus the carried over 1) = 4\n   - 6 \u00d7 3 = 18\n   - **Partial Product:** 1,848\n\n2. **Multiply 616 by 20 (tens place of 523):**\n   - 6 \u00d7 2 = 12\n   - 1 \u00d7 2 = 2 (plus the carried over 1) = 3\n   - 6 \u00d7 2 = 12\n   - **Partial Product:** 12,320\n\n3. **Multiply 616 by 500 (hundreds place of 523):**\n   - 6 \u00d7 5 = 30\n   - 1 \u00d7 5 = 5 (plus the carried over 3) = 8\n   - 6 \u00d7 5 = 30\n   - **Partial Product:** 308,000\n\n4. **Add all partial products together:**\n   - 1,848 + 12,320 = 14,168\n   - 14,168 + 308,000 = 322,168\n\n**Final Answer:** 322,168\n\nHowever, upon reviewing the initial thought, the correct product of 616 and 523 is actually 322,168, not 422,168.\n\n**Final Answer:** 322,168",
